# Impeccable Bolder Rules

Bolder does not mean louder.
It means clearer, more confident, and easier to scan.

---

## Core Principle

When in doubt, make it clearer.

Not more complex.
Not more decorative.
Clearer.

---

## Hierarchy

- Make important elements stand out
- Use:
  - larger text
  - stronger contrast
  - more spacing
- Avoid flat hierarchy where everything looks the same

---

## Contrast

- Ensure strong contrast between:
  - text and background
  - card and page
- Primary content must be clearly readable
- Avoid washed-out UI

---

## Spacing

- Increase spacing to improve clarity
- Use generous spacing between sections
- Avoid cramped layouts

---

## Size

- Make key elements bigger:
  - titles
  - images
  - CTA buttons
- Do not make everything bigger → only what matters

---

## Focus

- Limit attention points
- Each section should have 1 main focus
- Avoid multiple competing highlights

---

## Confidence

- Avoid "hesitant design":
  - small titles
  - weak contrast
  - unclear structure
- UI should feel intentional and decisive

---

## Constraints

- Do not change logic
- Do not change routes
- Maintain readability for beginners
- Keep design clean and minimal

---

## Goal

The UI should feel:

- clear
- confident
- easy to scan
- visually structured
